AirPort Extreme driver for Mac OS 9 -- credits and provenance
=============================================================

This is an independent, unofficial driver. It was built by studying and adapting the
following free/open implementations of the Broadcom BCM4306 radio and of WPA2. It is
released under the GNU General Public License v2 (see LICENSE), in recognition of the
GPL-licensed sources it draws on.

Reverse-engineering and port references
---------------------------------------
* Linux b43 / b43legacy  (GPL-2.0)
    drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/ -- BCM43xx PHY and radio bring-up, the DMA ring
    geometry, and MAC / microcode handling.
* FreeBSD / OpenBSD / DragonFly BSD  bwi(4)  (BSD-2-Clause)
    The reference implementation for this exact card (BCM4306, "v3" firmware), and the
    source of the firmware-fetch instructions in firmware/README.md.
* Linux mac80211  (GPL-2.0)
    Scan excursion timing and the power-save null-frame handshake.
* hostapd / wpa_supplicant, the hostap project  (BSD)
    WPA2-Personal: PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA1, the 4-way-handshake key derivation (PTK/GTK) and
    CCMP, adapted for the G4.

Firmware
--------
Broadcom BCM4306 microcode is proprietary to Broadcom and is NOT distributed here. See
firmware/README.md for how to obtain it -- the same position the Linux distributions and
the BSD ports take.

